Subject: [PATCH 1/3] The second screen: four changes to the anneal, read
 against lambda_then_w

greg chose at 16:52 UTC on 2026-10-30 to build four arms after the demo,
as blocks with tests and a frozen plan for a second screen; bordercall
8e966e4 holds them (schedule=cyclic, schedule=adaptive,
ladder=overlapping, restraint=abf, each changing nothing where it is
not named), and this brings them here and plans their screen. At 18:05
UTC, going into the operating room, he asked for whatever a training
run on gold tier 3 needs while he is out.

The copy under grid/autoanatomist/ is bordercall 8e966e4 (tools/
bordercall_vendor.py copy). Two plans: gold3_latent_smoke2, the five
anneals in series on the first smoke's four CTs, so the new blocks run
on a card before twelve trials take one each; and gold3_latent_screen2,
lambda_then_w as the null, cyclic, adaptive, overlapping, restraint and
ct_only (the first screen's null under its own name), two seeds each, on
the first screen's own rows. tools/autoanatomist_plan.py takes the rows
from the committed plans (rows_of) and writes only the plans --plan
names, so the frozen plans keep their bytes.

PREREG.md gains section 8, which says the arms, the hypotheses, the
second smoke and four known limits, and is frozen a fourth time with the
two plans on its Covers line; sections 1 to 6 and the first two plans'
bytes are unchanged. A send copies the code at the gate's commit, so a
plan sent before this commit runs afe1952's copy, and each screen reads
its arms against a null trained at its own commit.

The gate counts both plans and orders them: the second smoke after the
first, the second screen after the second smoke. The report says the
second smoke answers no hypothesis and restates section 8's limits for
the second screen's plans; its DESIGN is the new PREREG sha256.

